<Base title="3/8 inch quick-connect" description="3/8 inch quick-connect fittings are common on pressure-washer hoses and spray-gun inlets. They do not accept 1/4 inch nozzle plugs." path="/qc-38/">
  <div class="prose">
    <p class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/quick-connect/">Quick-connect</a> / 3/8″</p>
    <h1>3/8″ quick-connect</h1>
    <Answer>
      Larger plug, larger flow. Used where a hose or gun would otherwise be M22. A 1/4″ nozzle will rattle in this socket and will not lock.
    </Answer>
    <p>If you convert a gas machine off M22, the usual stack is:</p>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li>M22-14 mm (or 15 mm) × 3/8″ QC on the pump.</li>
      <li>3/8″ QC hose.</li>
      <li>3/8″ QC × gun inlet (M22 or 3/8″ NPT, depending on the gun).</li>
      <li>1/4″ QC only after the gun, on the wand.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>Buy couplers stamped for your PSI. A 3/8″ socket from a farm store may be an air fitting. Test-fit a known washer hose plug before you run water.</p>
    <p><a href="/qc-14-vs-38/">1/4 vs 3/8</a> · <a href="/m22-to-quick-connect/">M22 conversion</a></p>
  </div>
</Base>
